+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop in
+Hollin Bridge. It has four pages:
+
+- **Home** (`index.html`): a welcome, staff shelf notes and links onward.
+- **Books** (`books.html`): twelve invented titles across six genres, with a genre
+  filter. The selected genre is kept in the address bar (`?genre=Mystery`), so a
+  filtered view can be bookmarked or shared, and back and forward restore it.
+- **Events** (`events.html`): upcoming readings and events in date order. Events
+  before your local date are marked as past.
+- **Visit** (`visit.html`): opening hours, the address, directions, accessibility
+  information and a contact form. The form validates in the browser and does not
+  send anything, because this is a demo.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. It has no build step, no npm runtime
+dependencies and no external requests: fonts are system fonts, and images are
+inline SVG or local files.
+
+## Run it locally
+
+Serve the folder with any static server, for example:
+
+```sh
+npx serve -l 8080 .
+```
+
+or
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8080
+```
+
+Then open <http://localhost:8080/>.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests use Node's built-in test runner to drive headless Chrome through
+Playwright. Playwright must be installed globally, and Chrome is expected at
+`/usr/bin/google-chrome` unless `CHROME_PATH` is set.
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
+
+To run one file:
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node --test tests/books.test.js
+```
+
+## Formatting
+
+```sh
+npx prettier --check .
+```
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the one stylesheet.
+- `js/main.js`: the mobile navigation toggle, shared by every page.
+- `js/books.js`, `js/events.js`, `js/visit.js`: page-specific behaviour.
+- `tests/`: browser tests. `tests/helpers/server.js` starts the static server.
